From 7b84a805d15965ea86aaf4b7a947073865e403c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:17:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 108/270] ARM: switch the PL310 outer cache on

The firmware of the Toshiba AC100 leaves the 1 MB L2 cache of the Tegra 2
off, and nothing switched it on. Do so at boot, with the latencies of the
device tree, the shared attribute override (all memory is shareable now,
which older revisions would not cache otherwise) and prefetching, as Linux
does on Tegra 2. "arm_l2_cache false" in the kernel settings leaves it off.

The CP15 maintenance operations stop at the outer cache: clean and
invalidate it by physical address too for the SDMA buffers of sdhci and when
memory becomes uncached. Table walks are now outer cacheable after a
context switch as well, like with the boot loader's page tables, so that
they see the page table updates in the L2 cache.
